.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-LEARNING 1 "2026-09-20" "ShardPost 0.23.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-learning \- inspect and retry jobs of the learning queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl learning list
.RB [ \-account
.IR account ]
.RB [ \-state
.IR state ]
.RB [ \-limit
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-after
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl learning show
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I job-id
.br
.B shardpostctl learning retry
.RB [ \-confirm-repeat ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I job-id
.SH DESCRIPTION
When a user moves a message into the junk mailbox (or out of it),
IMAPSieve queues a learning job. A worker hands the message to the
configured program, for example a spam filter's learn command, retries
with backoff and gives up after
.I imapsieve.learning.max_attempts
attempts. These commands look at that queue and put a dead job back into
it.
.SS learning list
The queue, oldest job id first, with account, program, state, attempts
and the next attempt.
.B \-state
narrows it to
.IR pending ,
.I dead
or
.IR delivered .
A client with an account scope must pass
.BR \-account .
Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS learning show
One job in detail: account, mailbox id, program, state, attempts, manual
retries, size, creation time and next attempt. The message itself is
never printed. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS learning retry
Makes a dead job due again: the attempt counter starts over and the
worker picks it up on its next pass.
.PP
Learning programs are not idempotent. A message learned twice counts
twice and skews the filter, and a job can be dead although its program
already received the message (a timeout after the handover, for example).
Therefore a job that was attempted before is only retried with
.BR \-confirm-repeat .
A job whose message was never committed to the store (no receipt) cannot
be retried at all: there is nothing left to learn.
.PP
Only dead jobs can be retried. A pending job is already scheduled, and a
delivered one is on its way out of the queue.
.PP
Role:
.BR repair .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-account " account"
Only jobs of this account.
.TP
.BI \-state " pending|dead|delivered"
Only jobs in this state.
.TP
.BI \-limit " n"
Jobs per page (up to 500).
.TP
.BI \-after " id"
Continue after this job id.
.TP
.B \-confirm-repeat
Retry although the program may already have seen this message.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
Is the queue backing up, and is anything dead?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl learning list -limit 20
shardpostctl learning list -state dead
.RE
.fi
.PP
A user says "marking as spam has no effect": look at their jobs.
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl learning list -account user@example.org
shardpostctl learning show 6f1c...e2
.RE
.fi
.PP
The spam filter was down for an hour. Put the jobs that died because of
it back into the queue, accepting that a message may be learned twice:
.PP
.nf
.RS
for id in $(shardpostctl learning list -state dead --json \\
        | jq -r '.items[].id'); do
    shardpostctl learning retry -confirm-repeat "$id"
done
.RE
.fi
.PP
A job that never reached its program (no attempt yet) needs no
confirmation:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl learning retry 6f1c...e2
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 65
The job is not dead, its message was never committed, or it was attempted
and
.B \-confirm-repeat
was not given.
.TP
.B 67
No such learning job.
.TP
.B 75
The learning queue is not available on this server.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role, or the job belongs to an account outside its
scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-sieve (1)
.PP
The learning rules are described in
.IR docs/imapsieve.md .
